{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s27-p01",
      "text": "Do you yawn?",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p02",
      "text": "There are about 20 reasons that scientists think are possible for yawning after research.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p03",
      "text": "They do not know exactly why yawning happens, but they do know many facts about yawning.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p04",
      "text": "Everyone yawns in the same way, from babies to adults.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p04.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p05",
      "text": "First you open your mouth slowly, like a sleepy lion.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p06",
      "text": "Your mouth stays open for about five seconds.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p06.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p07",
      "text": "You take in a lot of air and then push it out.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p08",
      "text": "Then you quickly close your mouth.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p09",
      "text": "Yawning is contagious.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p10",
      "text": "If you see someone yawn, your body may reply by yawning too, much like a secret way of communication.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p10.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p10.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p11",
      "text": "Many people say they yawn because they are tired.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p12",
      "text": "That might be true.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p12.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p12.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p13",
      "text": "People do often yawn before they sleep and after they wake up or before breakfast.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p14",
      "text": "However, people also yawn when they are excited or nervous.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p15",
      "text": "Yawning doesn't just mean you are lazy.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p15.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p16",
      "text": "Yawning proves that your body needs to stay alert.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p17",
      "text": "When you yawn, you breathe deeply.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p17.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p17.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p18",
      "text": "You also stretch the muscles in your face, throat, neck and shoulders.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p18.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p18.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p19",
      "text": "Your eardrums stretch, too.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p19.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p19.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p20",
      "text": "Maybe this helps you to be quicker to notice things.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p20.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p20.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p21",
      "text": "In some countries, people think yawning is not nice.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p21.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p21.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p22-01",
      "text": "People put their hands over their mouths to cover a yawn,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p22-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p22-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p22-02",
      "text": "and we often do the same thing when we cough.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p22-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p22-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p23",
      "text": "However, in other countries, people think yawning can let good things in.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p23.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p23.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p24",
      "text": "Scientists do not spend much time studying yawning.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p24.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p24.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p25",
      "text": "That is probably because yawning does not hurt or cause any medical emergency.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p25.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p25.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27-p26",
      "text": "It is just a normal thing we do.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p26.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s27-p26.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
